1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Excel is already open with repro.xlsx and the standalone add-in loaded.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Two copies of 15 argument sets. Earlier healthy recalculations are omitted.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:22,000
I click Read cell states. The public reader reports no Busy cells.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The streaming handler immediately calls setResult with the supplied code.
There is no data fetch, cache, timer or promise in the handler.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Expected: every formula resolves to its code after recalculation,
with no calculating icon left behind.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:53,500
I return focus to the worksheet, then request a full recalculation.

7
00:00:53,500 --> 00:01:00,000
Ctrl+Alt+F9: recalculate every formula.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:17,800
Both GP cells retain calculating icons: B10 and B26.
I stop recalculating and leave the worksheet untouched.

9
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:28,000
I click Read cell states again.
The add-in reads Excel Range.valuesAsJson.

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,300
Excel reports Busy in B10 and B26, although both still display GP.

11
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:51,400
B10 contains =REPRO.MEMBER("Account","GP").
It should resolve to the string GP.

12
00:01:51,400 --> 00:02:07,800
B26 has the identical formula. Both copies still show calculating icons.

13
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:18,000
I read again, 74 seconds after the last recalculation.
The public reader still reports Busy in both cells.

14
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Expected: both formulas resolve. Actual: both remain Busy.
Excel for Windows 16.0.20430.20092. The failure is intermittent.
